Package: csestudy
Type: Package
Title: Time-Series Inference for Cross-Sectional Event Studies
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jonathan B.", "Cohn", role = "aut"),
    person("Travis L.", "Johnson", role = "aut"),
    person("Zack", "Liu", role = "aut"),
    person("Malcolm I.", "Wardlaw", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "malcolm.wardlaw@uga.edu"))
Description: Implements the time-series approach to cross-sectional event-study
    inference of Cohn, Johnson, Liu and Wardlaw (2026)
    <doi:10.1016/j.jfineco.2026.104278>. The event-period cross-sectional
    relationship is benchmarked against a distribution of the same relationship
    estimated on pre-event days, using either ordinary least squares or
    generalized least squares with a principal-component covariance estimate.
    Rejection is summarised by an empirical cumulative-distribution-function
    p-value and a parametric p-value.
